[Al]-Sadr had called for a huge march in Baghdad to mark the[ anniversary] of Hussein's ouster and to protest the[ U].S. presence and al-Mal[iki]'s offensive. The cleric says the offensive, which began March 25 in the southern city of Basra, is targeting his Mah[di] Army and is a ploy to cripple his political movement in advance of provincial elections planned for October.
